 "result": "Look at how the login check is registered in your admin bundle. It's almost certainly decorated with `@admin.before_any_request`.\n\n**Why:**\n- `Bundle.before_any_request` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:614`) doesn't scope to the bundle. It appends the function to `app.before_request_funcs[None]`, the app-wide key (line 619). That's the same as `app.before_request`, so it runs for every request, whichever bundle handles it.\n- `Scaffold.before_request` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:468`) is the bundle-scoped one. Used on a bundle, it runs only for requests that bundle handles. At registration, `bundles.py:402` merges the bundle's `before_request_funcs` under the bundle's name.\n\n**Fix:** Change `@admin.before_any_request` to `@admin.before_request`. If the check should also run for the app's other bundles, put it on the app explicitly instead.\n\nAlso check that the admin bundle's `before_request` handlers don't return a non-`None` value (such as a redirect to login) from an app-wide hook. `preprocess_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1366`) short-circuits on any non-`None` return, so that would block every route, including the login page itself.",
